WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.090
In China's Badain Jaran Desert, star
dunes reach up to 500 metres high.

2
00:00:06.140 --> 00:00:10.910
In Ningxia Province, some crescent
dunes moved more than 100 metres a year,

3
00:00:10.960 --> 00:00:13.890
from 1954 to 59.

4
00:00:13.940 --> 00:00:17.430
That's the desert most
of us picture: sand.

5
00:00:17.480 --> 00:00:21.450
Yet sand covers only about 20
per cent of Earth's deserts.

6
00:00:21.500 --> 00:00:25.450
In Death Valley, California,
dunes cover less than 1 per cent.

7
00:00:25.500 --> 00:00:27.070
So what shapes the rest?

8
00:00:27.120 --> 00:00:28.950
Wind alone?

9
00:00:29.000 --> 00:00:29.910
Ice?

10
00:00:29.960 --> 00:00:33.230
In this mission, you'll
see how wind lifts dust,

11
00:00:33.280 --> 00:00:37.570
bounces and rolls sand, and
how a dune moves downwind.

12
00:00:37.620 --> 00:00:40.830
Then you'll read mesas,
buttes and rock pedestals,

13
00:00:40.880 --> 00:00:44.150
where the textbook explanation
has been challenged.

14
00:00:44.200 --> 00:00:49.480
Your mission: explain what shapes the
desert surfaces that sand does not cover.
